answer:
To show a "Make Profile Public" option when signing up, you need to modify the code that determines whether a member's account is set as public or private. 

In your case, since the checkbox for members to choose profile privacy on signup is automatically selected for a public profile, it appears that the default behavior is already in place. However, you can still add a "Make Profile Public" option when signing up.

You would need to update the code in your site's admin panel or backend to check if the member has unchecked the "Members can select or deselect the checkbox to allow their profile to be public" checkbox. If it is checked, then set the member's account as private by default.

Here's a possible solution:

```php
if (isset($_POST['make_profile_public'])) {
    // Check if the member has selected public profile
    $publicProfile = $_POST['public_profile'];

    // If they have not selected public profile, set them to private
    if (!$publicProfile) {
        $_SESSION['account_privacy'] = 'private';

        // Redirect to login page after setting account privacy
        header('Location: login.php');
        exit;
    }
}
```

Then, when the member signs up and selects "Make Profile Public" from the dropdown menu, you would update their account settings to private:

```php
public_profile = $_POST['make_profile_public'];
AccountSettings->Privacy = 'private';
AccountSettings->Save();
```

Please note that this solution assumes that your site is using a backend (e.g. PHP) and not just a frontend with an admin panel. Also, you would need to adjust the code to fit your specific use case.
